{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_vrtx_011Cg4X3PRnbMq3tV2YfxHec", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I fixed the WAL file and recovered all 11 records into `/app/recovered.json`, sorted by id.\n\n**The cause:** every byte of `main.db-wal` had been XORed with `0x42`. The giveaway was the long runs of `B` (0x42) where there should have been zero bytes. Also, the first four bytes `75 3d 44 c0` XOR `0x42` come out as `37 7f 06 82`, which is the normal start of a WAL file.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Decoded the WAL by XORing it with `0x42` again, and tested it on a copy of the database first. With the decoded WAL, SQLite reads it fine and `PRAGMA integrity_check` returns `ok`.\n2. Pulled out all rows from the `items` table, including the changes in the WAL:\n\n| id | name | value |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | apple | 150 |\n| 2 | banana | 250 |\n| 3 | cherry | 300 |\n| 4 | date | 400 |\n| 5 | elderberry | 500 |\n| 6 | fig | 600 |\n| 7 | grape | 700 |\n| 8 | honeydew | 800 |\n| 9 | kiwi | 900 |\n| 10 | lemon | 1000 |\n| 11 | mango | 1100 |\n\n3. Wrote the decoded WAL back to `/app/main.db-wal`, replacing the scrambled one. I left `/app/main.db` untouched, so SQLite will apply the WAL changes the next time it opens the database.\n\nThe output is in the format you asked for, e.g. `[{\"id\": 1, \"name\": \"apple\", \"value\": 150}, ...]`.\n\nThe scrambled original WAL isn't kept anywhere. I made a backup but deleted it once the decoded version was written. Applying the same XOR to the current file gets it back if you ever need it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1352, "cache_read_input_tokens": 17778, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1352, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 614}, "input_transformations": [], "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3de8d14f-ff3b-4bd6-a8e0-861489c76236", "uuid": "566ddbfc-57ff-4648-bef9-07382e1c51d0", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T18:45:42.940Z", "request_id": "req_vrtx_011Cg4X3PQ3SZ1WCYtyBzVLF"}
